id: pm-s4y3z4
title: "The docs gate enforces link resolution but not doc reachability, so orphaned docs pass CI and the advertised docs map silently drifts"
description: "docs-skills-gate.mjs validates that relative markdown links resolve, but has no inverse check for docs nothing links to. docs/PR_REVIEW_LOOP.md has zero inbound links repo-wide; docs/PERFORMANCE.md and docs/RELATIONSHIP_GRAPH.md are absent from docs/README.md, the file AGENTS.md advertises as the full docs map."
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 3
tags[5]: agent-ux,ci-gate,docs,progressive-disclosure,repo-organization
created_at: "2026-07-26T18:28:37.877Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T07:10:20.384Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "The docs gate fails when a docs/*.md file is not reachable from docs/README.md, directly or transitively; An explicit opt-out list covers deliberately standalone docs so the gate is narrowed rather than silenced; docs/PR_REVIEW_LOOP.md, docs/PERFORMANCE.md and docs/RELATIONSHIP_GRAPH.md are each linked, opted out, or removed"
goal: project management = context management
value: "Keeps the advertised progressive-disclosure map and the on-disk docs tree in agreement automatically, instead of after each manual audit."
impact: Under a progressive-disclosure navigation model an unlinked doc is invisible to the agent it was written for while still costing review and maintenance.
outcome: "A reachability pass in the docs gate with an explicit opt-out list, and the three current orphans linked, listed, or removed."
why_now: pm-c97q closed the same class by hand-adding two links and added no enforcement; the class has already recurred with three different files.
parent: pm-kb5h
risk: low
confidence: high
dependencies[3]{id,kind,created_at}:
  pm-c97q,discovered_from,"2026-07-26T18:29:22.905Z"
  pm-yh8r,related,"2026-07-26T18:29:22.905Z"
  pm-u9d0,implements,"2026-07-27T07:10:20.163Z"
body: "## Problem\n\nThe docs gate checks that markdown links **resolve**. It does not check that\ndocs are **reachable**. Those are different properties, and only the first is\nenforced, so a doc that nothing links to passes CI forever.\n\nscripts/release/docs-skills-gate.mjs validates \"relative markdown links in docs\n+ README/AGENTS/CONTRIBUTING\" — i.e. it catches a link pointing at a file that\ndoes not exist (dangling link). It has no inverse check for a file that exists\nand that no index points at (orphaned doc).\n\n## Evidence 2026-07-26\n\nAGENTS.md advertises docs/README.md as the \"Full docs map\" and the progressive\ndisclosure entrypoint. Measured against the actual docs/ tree:\n\n| doc | in docs/README.md map | inbound links repo-wide |\n|---|---|---|\n| docs/PR_REVIEW_LOOP.md | no | **0** |\n| docs/PERFORMANCE.md | no | 1 |\n| docs/RELATIONSHIP_GRAPH.md | no | 2 |\n\ndocs/PR_REVIEW_LOOP.md is referenced by zero markdown files anywhere in the\nrepository. It is unreachable by any agent following the documented navigation\npath, and unreachable by any human browsing the docs index.\n\n## Why this is a gate gap, not a re-file of pm-c97q\n\npm-c97q (CLOSED, Chore) was \"Docs index missing EXTENSION_AUTHOR_CONTRACTS +\nMIGRATION_CLI_SIMPLIFICATION links\". It fixed the two instances that existed at\nthe time by adding two links. It did not add an enforcement, so the class\nrecurred with three different files. Re-adding three links would reproduce the\nsame outcome a third time.\n\nThis item owns the enforcement: docs/README.md is a hand-maintained index over\na directory that changes, and hand-maintained indexes drift by default.\n\n## Why it matters more here than in a typical repo\n\nThe project's stated navigation model is progressive disclosure: AGENTS.md is\ndeliberately short and routes to docs/ via the map. An unlinked doc is not\nmerely untidy — under that model it is invisible to the agent the doc was\nwritten for, while still costing review and maintenance. It also directly feeds\nthe \"the repo is getting confusing\" symptom, because the on-disk tree and the\nadvertised map disagree with no signal that they do.\n\n## Direction (not a mandate for the fix)\n\nExtend docs-skills-gate.mjs with a reachability pass: every docs/*.md must be\nlinked from docs/README.md or from another doc reachable from it, with an\nexplicit opt-out list for deliberately standalone files so the gate stays\nhonest rather than being silenced wholesale. Then reconcile the three current\norphans — link them, or record them on the opt-out list, or delete\nPR_REVIEW_LOOP.md if it is superseded."
